# Thresholding — pick a method from the dropdown; its own parameters appear
# below automatically via params().
#
# Adding a new algorithm with Category()=="threshold" makes it show up here
# with its controls, without editing this script at all.
#
# A note on what you will see, because it is easy to misread as a bug.
#
# test.png is a smooth gradient with a checkerboard patch. Its local standard
# deviation is 3-11 across the gradient and 127 inside the patch, so a LOCAL
# method has almost nothing to find outside that corner and correctly returns
# nearly uniform white. The global methods (otsu, triangle, isodata) are the
# interesting ones here.
#
# To see what the local methods are for, drop a scanned page on the "test" row
# -- or use the synthetic one:
#
#   ./build/Release/tglab.exe scripts/thresholds.tgl assets/page.png
#
# and change image("test") below to image("page"). That fixture is text under
# uneven lighting, bright top left falling to dim bottom right. No single global
# level serves both ends: measured, the five local methods recover the text
# perfectly while otsu manages 66%.

src = image("test")

op = choose("method", "threshold")

blur  = slider("blur sigma", 0.0, 8.0, 0.0)
blurred = gaussian_blur(src, sigma = blur)

mask = params(op)(blurred)

display(src,     "1 source")
display(blurred, "2 blurred")
display(mask,    "3 mask")
